   "capture.json": "825e8f5354e65f80c405b87fbdac749bd658f1068b3975bb5adc048f3a9ae229"
  },
  "capture_notes": [
   "decode[].decoded is a verbatim copy of the handlePoW decode step (json.NewDecoder over http.MaxBytesReader(4096)); decode[].response is the real handlePoW reply for the same body on a session with no issued challenge",
   "decode[].pads expand, in order, each @PAD@ token of body to len copies of byte; body_hex carries bodies that are not valid UTF-8",
   "decoded.nonce_hex is the hex of the decoded nonce bytes; nonces longer than 64 bytes are recorded as nonce_len plus nonce_sha256",
   "issue_header and handle ran against one collector.Store at now_unix; the challenge bucket is now_unix / 120 (the capture retried until the bucket did not roll over)",
   "handle[].after.last_signal is the last network signal stored by the handler; an l7.pow.too_fast value (elapsed wall-clock milliseconds) is replaced by <elapsed_ms>",
   "handle verdict and riskScore come from the Go scoring engine on the stored report; the Rust test feeds them back as the injected scorer result and compares everything else",
   "read_file ran in a fresh temporary directory: a.txt, empty.bin, directory sub, symlinks link.txt -> a.txt, linkdir -> sub, dangling -> missing; not_exist is errors.Is(err, os.ErrNotExist)",
   "ja4_stable[].hello is the Go network.ClientHello value (null for no ClientHello)"
  ]
 },
